    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 58 ('Hooligan Bullies! (the live random encounter: hooligan bullies)'): scene sg_random_encounter_01, entry, exit, 3 waves, 10 spawns ({'Hooligan': 7, 'Hooligan Archer': 2, 'Hooligan Scrapper': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1239 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_01 has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 15 coins / 100 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "The quest step and the wiki put 'Hooligan Bullies!' in this fight; the fork's layout had 'hooligan' there. (R) 'Hooligan Bullies!' takes those spots (wiki over the fork's roster)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): model 203 human_m_hooligan_brawler_01.agr (the Hooligan's body); the fight's waves field this kind, and 1913 sg_spawner_human_01.adr is the battle starter's tent prop (Legacy NPC 4162), not a fighter."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): this row is the battle's starter, the prop 2014 drew it as (the Snarler's den: video 5-IM2pBh2yY frames 01048 and 01080, red name, crossed swords, Press X; capture p12 t=546051.7 model 1938). The fight's own kind carries the body its waves fight with."
    }
